# Focused Cuckoo vs Robin Hood comparison commands.
#
# Each line is:
#   ./benchmark_cuckoo_robin <input> <n> <3n> <total_slots> <maxLoop> \
#                            <maxRehashSafety> <algo> <interrupt_cycles>
#
# `algo` may be cuckoo, robinhood (alias: robin), or both.
# Same equilibrium workload as Pagh & Rodler §4.4: n inserts then 3n rounds of
# {unsuccessful lookup, successful lookup, delete, insert}. total_slots = 4n
# keeps the steady-state load factor at ~1/4.
#
# To average across 10 runs, drive these via:
#   python3 run_benchmark_commands.py \
#       --commands-file docs/commands_cuckoo_robin \
#       --output docs/cuckoo_robin_results.csv --runs 10
